[RESULT]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Correctness            : PASSED AT ALL CORRECTION LEVELS
  Current-state trend    : Pre-compaction speedup fell from 2.22x at 0% corrected to 1.02x at 50% corrected.
  Historical AS OF trend : At 50% corrected (7,553 versions over 5,010 keys), AS OF speedup vs. the row-wise scan ranged 1.02x (cutoff showing 100% of versions) to 238.09x (cutoff showing 0% of versions) across 6 cutoffs; the primary mid-history cutoff (50% of versions visible) gave 1.98x with 49.37% of chunks pruned.
  Compaction trend       : Runtime grew from 11.771 ms at 1% corrected to 263.779 ms at 50% corrected.
  Result artifact        : /home/abc/Desktop/Resume Projects/PitDB/benchmarks/results/bitemporal_sweep.json

  Interpretation
    Historical AS OF queries can reject correction chunks whose transaction
    times occur after the requested cutoff. The pruning and speedup actually
    obtained depend on how many correction versions the cutoff leaves visible
    (see the AS OF sweep tables and the trend line above); no single AS OF
    speedup describes every cutoff.

  Limitation
    Performance conclusions apply only to the tested synthetic correction
    model (random lags of 1-90 days, up to 3 versions per key, 20 symbols, 501
    rows each) and compaction policy.

